course: dictionary
lesson: 10949
title: Wait: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Wait is a small word with many jobs. Most often it means to stay where you are until something happens or someone comes. «We had to wait for the bus for fifteen minutes.» The bus had not come yet, so you stayed put.
explain: Wait can also be a noun, meaning the time you spend waiting. «There was a long wait at the doctor's.» In maths, a wait can be the time between two clock times, such as from 3:10 to 3:45, which is 35 minutes.
explain: In casual talk, wait can work differently. «No wait, that's six!» means the speaker is correcting a number, so the last number counts. «Hang on» and «hold your horses» also mean wait. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: the context leaves clues.
fact: Wait means to stay where you are, or hold off doing something, until something happens.
fact: A wait is the time you spend waiting, as in «a long wait».
fact: «Can't wait» means you are very excited about something that is coming soon.
fact: To wait on people means to serve them food, as in a restaurant.
fact: Formal words for wait include «await», as in «Passengers awaited the service for 15 minutes.»
exercise: «Time feels shorter when you are playing and longer when you are waiting.» In this sentence, what does waiting mean? | Singing loudly | Sleeping in bed | Running very fast | *Staying where you are until something happens
exercise: Maya says, «We had a wait of 35 minutes between the two trains.» What is a wait here? | A kind of station | A train ticket | A loud noise | *The time spent waiting
exercise: Sam says, «Mum has 5 biscuits, no wait, 6!» What does «no wait» do? | It means Sam is tired | It means the biscuits are all gone | *It corrects the number, so 6 is right | It means stop eating now
test: «Passengers awaited the service for 15 minutes.» What does awaited mean? | Forgot | Ran from | Paid for | *Waited for
test: A waiter in a restaurant is someone who does what? | Sits still all day | Cooks the food in the kitchen | Waits for the bus at the stop | *Waits on people by serving them food
exam: Which phrase means wait in casual talk? | Go to sleep | Run fast | *Hold your horses | Shout loudly
